@host = http://localhost:5085
@run = 1
@codeMarcelo = 000000
@codeJoao = 000000
@codePedro = 000000
@codeLucas = 000000

### 1a. Marcelo pede o código (o e-mail aparece no console da API)
# Copie o código de 6 dígitos do console para @codeMarcelo, no topo do arquivo.
# Para rodar o fluxo de novo do zero, troque @run (cada rodada usa e-mails novos).
POST {{host}}/api/auth/email/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "marcelo.{{run}}@example.com" }

### 1b. Marcelo confirma o código e recebe os tokens
# @name loginMarcelo
POST {{host}}/api/auth/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "marcelo.{{run}}@example.com", "code": "{{codeMarcelo}}" }

### 1c. Marcelo cria o perfil (devolve um token novo, já com o player_id)
# @name marcelo
POST {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMarcelo.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Marcelo" }

### 2a. João pede o código
POST {{host}}/api/auth/email/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "joao.{{run}}@example.com" }

### 2b. João confirma o código
# @name loginJoao
POST {{host}}/api/auth/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "joao.{{run}}@example.com", "code": "{{codeJoao}}" }

### 2c. João cria o perfil
# @name joao
POST {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginJoao.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "João" }

### 3a. Pedro pede o código
POST {{host}}/api/auth/email/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "pedro.{{run}}@example.com" }

### 3b. Pedro confirma o código
# @name loginPedro
POST {{host}}/api/auth/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "pedro.{{run}}@example.com", "code": "{{codePedro}}" }

### 3c. Pedro cria o perfil
# @name pedro
POST {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginPedro.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Pedro" }

### 4a. Lucas pede o código
# O login aceita 10 requisições por minuto: se vier 429, espere um minuto.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/email/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "lucas.{{run}}@example.com" }

### 4b. Lucas confirma o código
# @name loginLucas
POST {{host}}/api/auth/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "lucas.{{run}}@example.com", "code": "{{codeLucas}}" }

### 4c. Lucas cria o perfil
# @name lucas
POST {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLucas.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Lucas" }

### 5. Marcelo vê o próprio perfil
GET {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}

### 6. Marcelo cria o grupo e vira o presidente (entra como mensalista e no rodízio)
# @name group
POST {{host}}/api/groups
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Teste manual", "playersPerTeam": 2, "benchPlayersPerTeam": 0, "matchDay": "Tuesday" }

### 7. O presidente adiciona os membros
POST {{host}}/api/groups/{{group.response.body.$.id}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "playerId": "{{joao.response.body.$.player.id}}", "type": "Regular" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/groups/{{group.response.body.$.id}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "playerId": "{{pedro.response.body.$.player.id}}", "type": "Substitute" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/groups/{{group.response.body.$.id}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "playerId": "{{lucas.response.body.$.player.id}}", "type": "Substitute" }

### 8. O presidente cria a dupla Marcelo + João
POST {{host}}/api/groups/{{group.response.body.$.id}}/pairs
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstPlayerId": "{{marcelo.response.body.$.player.id}}", "secondPlayerId": "{{joao.response.body.$.player.id}}" }

### 9. O presidente cria a temporada (6 meses)
# @name season
POST {{host}}/api/groups/{{group.response.body.$.id}}/seasons
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "2026/2", "start": "2026-07-01" }

### 10. O presidente abre a lista (mensalistas aparecem em "pending")
# @name list
POST {{host}}/api/groups/{{group.response.body.$.id}}/lists
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "matchDate": "2026-10-20" }

### 11. Cada um confirma a própria presença
POST {{host}}/api/lists/{{list.response.body.$.id}}/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "positions": ["Defender"] }

###
POST {{host}}/api/lists/{{list.response.body.$.id}}/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{joao.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "positions": ["Midfielder", "Forward"] }

###
POST {{host}}/api/lists/{{list.response.body.$.id}}/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{pedro.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "positions": ["Goalkeeper"] }

###
POST {{host}}/api/lists/{{list.response.body.$.id}}/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{lucas.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "positions": ["Forward"] }

### 12. Lucas muda a própria posição
PUT {{host}}/api/lists/{{list.response.body.$.id}}/entries/me
Authorization: Bearer {{lucas.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "positions": ["Forward", "Midfielder"] }

### 13. Pedro vê a lista (4 em "playing", 0 vagas abertas)
GET {{host}}/api/lists/{{list.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{pedro.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}

### 14. O presidente fecha a lista
POST {{host}}/api/lists/{{list.response.body.$.id}}/close
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}

### 15. O presidente inicia a escalação (professor: Marcelo; parceiro: João)
# @name lineup
POST {{host}}/api/lists/{{list.response.body.$.id}}/lineup
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}

### 16. O professor da vez (Marcelo) divide os outros jogadores
PUT {{host}}/api/lineups/{{lineup.response.body.$.id}}/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "teamA": ["{{pedro.response.body.$.player.id}}"], "teamB": ["{{lucas.response.body.$.player.id}}"] }

### 17. A dupla do professor (João) escolhe o time A; o professor vai para o B
POST {{host}}/api/lineups/{{lineup.response.body.$.id}}/choice
Authorization: Bearer {{joao.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "team": "A" }

### 18. O professor registra o resultado (time A venceu)
# @name match
POST {{host}}/api/lineups/{{lineup.response.body.$.id}}/match
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "goalsA": 3, "goalsB": 1 }

### 19. Ranking (João e Pedro em 1º com 3 pontos)
GET {{host}}/api/seasons/{{season.response.body.$.id}}/ranking
Authorization: Bearer {{lucas.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}

### 20. Grupo: Marcelo foi para o fim do rodízio
GET {{host}}/api/groups/{{group.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{joao.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}

### 21. Renovar a sessão do Marcelo (o refresh token antigo deixa de valer)
# @name refreshMarcelo
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{loginMarcelo.response.body.$.refreshToken}}" }

### 22. Sair (logout): o refresh token novo é revogado
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshMarcelo.response.body.$.refreshToken}}" }

### Erros: sem token → 401
GET {{host}}/api/groups/{{group.response.body.$.id}}

### Erros: logado, mas sem perfil (token do login, sem player_id) → 403 "Profile required"
GET {{host}}/api/groups/{{group.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginPedro.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Erros: quem não é o professor da vez tenta montar os times → 403
PUT {{host}}/api/lineups/{{lineup.response.body.$.id}}/teams
Authorization: Bearer {{pedro.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "teamA": ["{{pedro.response.body.$.player.id}}"], "teamB": ["{{lucas.response.body.$.player.id}}"] }

### Erros: quem não é o presidente tenta corrigir o placar → 403
PUT {{host}}/api/matches/{{match.response.body.$.id}}/score
Authorization: Bearer {{joao.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "goalsA": 0, "goalsB": 1 }

### Erros: refresh token já usado → 401 (e todos os tokens do Marcelo são revogados)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{loginMarcelo.response.body.$.refreshToken}}" }

### Erros: código errado → 400 "Invalid code"
POST {{host}}/api/auth/email/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "pedro.{{run}}@example.com", "code": "123456" }

### Erros: abrir de novo a lista da mesma data → 409
POST {{host}}/api/groups/{{group.response.body.$.id}}/lists
Authorization: Bearer {{marcelo.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "matchDate": "2026-10-20" }

### Erros: inscrição sem posição → 400 com "errors"
POST {{host}}/api/lists/{{list.response.body.$.id}}/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{pedro.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "positions": [] }

### Erros: confirmar presença na lista fechada → 422
POST {{host}}/api/lists/{{list.response.body.$.id}}/entries
Authorization: Bearer {{pedro.response.body.$.token.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "positions": ["Forward"] }

### Documento OpenAPI
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json
